# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Luma — cmakelint Configuration
#
# Static-analysis settings for CMake files. Applied by the CMake CI gate
# (.github/workflows/ci-cmake.yml) and any local
# `cmakelint --config=.cmakelintrc` run.
#
# Two built-in checks are disabled because they conflict with the project's
# documented CMake conventions (instructions/cmake.instructions.md), not
# because the files violate good style:
#
#   linelength        cmakelint measures width in UTF-8 bytes, so the
#                     box-drawing character (U+2500 '─') used throughout the
#                     project's comment-header separators counts as three units
#                     each and trips the limit on lines that are well under 100
#                     visible columns. Column width is already declared per file
#                     by .editorconfig (max_line_length = 100).
#
#   whitespace/indent cmakelint assumes 2-space indentation; the project uses
#                     4 spaces (enforced by .editorconfig), which the check
#                     reports as "weird indentation".
#
# Every other built-in check still runs: command casing
# (readability/mixedcase), tabs, trailing whitespace, parenthesis spacing, and
# syntax.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

filter=-linelength,-whitespace/indent
